//! What is lit, as a renderer takes it: the G-buffer (its depth, settled
//! from a rough one while the lens moves, the layer seen through glass, a
//! ray walked across it), two G-buffers made one, decals pressed into it
//! and outlines drawn from it; the coarse scene light is traced through
//! (proxies baked from things' own distances or from a mesh, walked
//! roughly along a ray); and meshes drawn into it as clusters, streamed
//! round the lens.
package surface@1 { language = 2; ir = 1; }

use "kernels/";
